\frametitle{Recovery at the qualified log-linear-pool corner}

This nested limit is useful for interpretation. The \(c\to0\) limit
identifies the aggregation family with a known consensus operator; the
\(\lambda=1.0\) slice identifies the objective-backed implementation
used in the main server comparison. Neither limit grants the server-side
\breaktt{robust\_aggregate} heuristic a variational objective or a
bounded-influence guarantee. The FedGVI literature's rate and robustness
results remain attached to their stated loss, divergence, and sampling
assumptions (Mildner, Hamelijnck, et al. 2025; Mildner, Giampouras, et
al. 2025).
